>>
Rule 1 (input tensor must be at least 2-D so a lower triangle over the last two axes is defined)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 2
>>
Rule 2 (tensor dtype must be boolean, numeric, or complex; strings are not allowed)
{v_1 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) = 0 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 1 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 2 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 3 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 4 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 5 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 6 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 7 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 8 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 9 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 10
>>
Rule 3 (all batch dimensions, if any, must be valid non-negative sizes)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) > 2 then ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 3] : shape(v_1, i) ≥ 0
>>
Rule 5 (for non-empty matrices, k should be low enough to include at least one diagonal)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= if (∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = 0) then true else v_2 ≥ 1 - shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - 2)
>>
Rule 6 (for non-empty matrices, k should not exceed the last (column) dimension)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= if (∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = 0) then true else v_2 ≤ shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - 1) - 1
>>
Rule 7 (batch dimensions, if present, should be non-empty)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) ≥ 3 then ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 3] : shape(v_1, i) ≥ 1
>>
Rule 8 (either the input has an empty dimension or the last two dims form at least a 1×1 matrix)
{v_1 : tensor} |= (∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = 0) ∨ (shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - 2) ≥ 1 ∧ shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - 1) ≥ 1)
